{"reference":"2 Samuel 14","book":"2 Samuel","chapter":14,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"In the Larger Story","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Second Samuel’s larger story moves from David’s rise and the consolidation of his kingdom into accounts of royal abuse, violence within his household, rebellion, and grief. This chapter belongs within that later movement, where conflict in David’s family remains unresolved even as Absalom is brought back to Jerusalem.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_2_samuel_014_f8e6c842ae5cabdceb7e8943"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}